  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Rewriting the equation \\((2 x+y+2) a+(3 x-y-4) b=0\\) and for all \\(a\\), \\(\\mathrm{b}\\) the straight lines pass through the intersection of \\(2 x+y+2=0\\) and \\(3 x-y-4=0\\) i.e., the point \\(\\left(\\frac{2}{5},-\\frac{14}{5}\\right)\\).",
